# Security Rules

## General Security Principles

### Authentication

- Always require authentication for sensitive operations
- Verify user identity before granting access
- Use Firebase Auth tokens for user identification
- Implement proper session management
- Handle authentication state changes properly

### Authorization

- Implement role-based access control (RBAC)
- Check user permissions before operations
- Use proper user roles (admin, member, etc.)
- Implement organization-based access control
- Handle multi-tenant data properly

### Data Validation

- Validate all input data on both client and server
- Sanitize user inputs
- Use proper data types and formats
- Implement input length limits
- Validate file uploads and attachments

